{"format":1,"key":"zone:orgrimmar","path":"/lore/zone/orgrimmar","name":"Orgrimmar","kind":"zone","label":"Capital","zone":{"key":"orgrimmar","name":"Orgrimmar","path":"/lore/zone/orgrimmar"},"levels":"","description":"Orgrimmar rises from the red canyons of northern Durotar as the orcs’ fortified capital and the New Horde’s heart. Trolls, tauren, and Forsaken allies…","intro":[],"clips":[{"id":"zone:orgrimmar","part":"narration","anchor":"story","title":"The story","paras":["Orgrimmar rises from the red canyons of northern Durotar as the orcs’ fortified capital and the New Horde’s heart. Trolls, tauren, and Forsaken allies also find shelter within its walls.","Orgrimmar grew from the orcs’ search for a homeland after the Third War. Warchief Thrall led them to Kalimdor’s arid coasts, seeking freedom from demonic corruption and human bondage. He named the harsh land Durotar for his father and the city for his fallen mentor, Orgrim Doomhammer. Building the stronghold cost blood and sweat. With help from the tauren, Darkspear trolls, goblin engineers, and the Champion Rexxar, the Horde drove back centaur, harpies, and ferocious thunder lizards that threatened the canyons.","Rugged mountains shield Orgrimmar from foreign invaders and Durotar’s violent razor-winds. The city’s natural hollows give each valley its own place in Horde life. The Valley of Strength holds the civic gatehouse, with a route deeper into the trade bazaar of The Drag. Tauren druids and shaman gather by the pools in the Valley of Wisdom. Darkspear shadow hunters and witch doctors live among the stilted pavilions of the Valley of Spirits."],"hash":"9b8a7d","voices":{"male-narrator":{"sha":"f5f5f88577","sec":69},"female-narrator":{"sha":"5d51ff13af","sec":71}}}],"sources":[{"kind":"wiki","title":"Orgrimmar","url":"https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Orgrimmar"}],"related":[{"p":"/lore/npc/thrall","n":"Thrall","k":"npc"},{"p":"/lore/npc/orgrim-doomhammer","n":"Orgrim Doomhammer","k":"npc"},{"p":"/lore/zone/du